# SDL3's Android release, which `./fetch-sdl3.sh` downloads. 16 MB of binaries built against an NDK
# and an API level somebody else chose — the org's rule against carrying a prebuilt `.so` in a
# package, applied one level up.
app/libs/*.aar

# Gradle and AGP output.
.gradle/
build/
app/build/
app/.cxx/

# sbt's, which is a second build system and therefore a second output directory. Ninety-one of its
# files were committed before this line existed, which is the sort of thing nobody notices until
# somebody clones the repository to start from.
target/

# Written by Android Studio when it opens the project, and holds `sdk.dir` — an absolute path into
# somebody's home directory.
local.properties

# The IDE's own state.
.idea/
*.iml

# What `sysl build-c` writes beside your program: the archive CMake links, and the C header that
# describes what it exports. Both are build output that happens to land in a source directory.
program/*.a
program/*.a.h
